From aae495d2e56791213d3d2ad4acf9af7f4ecd966a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Leonardo Grasso <me@leonardograsso.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 18:58:09 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] feat(sandbox): add an unmediated-network boundary mode

Add --unmediated-network to openshell-sandbox, also accepted as the first
argument of launch-capability-free. With it, the workload listener no
longer forwards the eight network syscalls (socket, connect, bind, listen,
sendto, sendmsg, sendmmsg, setsockopt), so the kernel handles workload
sockets directly in the workload's network namespace. Signal and openat
mediation, Landlock, the main seccomp filter and the capability-free
identity are unchanged, and the boundary logs a warning when the mode is
on.

This is a local fork patch for yoloctl's opt-in unconfined network and
deliberately departs from RFC 0012's network invariants for boxes that use
it. The default stays fully mediated: start() and run() keep their
behaviour and signatures, and a test pins the mediated syscall list as
upstream ships it.

Signed-off-by: Leonardo Grasso <me@leonardograsso.com>
